{"name":"Koeksister","hex":"#e97551","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"koeksister","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A traditional Afrikaner confection consisting of a deep-fried twisted or plaited doughnut dipped in syrup immediately after cooking."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/koeksister"}],"entries":[{"title":"Koeksister","blocks":[{"text":"A koeksister is a traditional Afrikaner confectionery made of fried dough infused in syrup or honey. There is also a Cape Malay version of the dish, which is a fried ball of dough that is rolled in desiccated coconut called a koesister. The name derives from the Dutch and Afrikaans word \"koek\", which generally means a wheat flour confectionery."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Koeksisters.jpg/330px-Koeksisters.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koeksister","wikidata":"Q286829"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Koeksisters_shop_CT.jpg/120px-Koeksisters_shop_CT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Koeksisters_shop_CT.jpg/250px-Koeksisters_shop_CT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Koeksisters_shop_CT.jpg/120px-Koeksisters_shop_CT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKoeksisters_shop_CT.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Orania_Koeksuster_Sculpture_%284659267641%29_%282%29.jpg/120px-Orania_Koeksuster_Sculpture_%284659267641%29_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Orania_Koeksuster_Sculp